WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.550
This slide is the kit's own
design, not a Microsoft rule.

2
00:00:03.550 --> 00:00:06.800
In the kit, every check
has the same five parts.

3
00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:12.035
The catalog entry holds its I D, track,
title, source, Graph permissions,

4
00:00:12.035 --> 00:00:17.087
delegated role and release stage,
and marks it optional or preview.

5
00:00:17.087 --> 00:00:21.487
The function is named from the I
D, here Invoke V K Sync oh two,

6
00:00:21.487 --> 00:00:24.237
and wraps its body in a shared helper.

7
00:00:24.237 --> 00:00:27.893
The data read goes through
one path, for fixtures,

8
00:00:27.893 --> 00:00:31.913
Graph and input files, and
logs every read as evidence.

9
00:00:31.913 --> 00:00:35.375
The rows have one shape, and
the status comes from the rows.

10
00:00:35.375 --> 00:00:38.233
And the tests: the check
must pass clean data

11
00:00:38.233 --> 00:00:41.250
and fail planted problems
with an exact count.

12
00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:44.075
The wrapper does the work
no check should repeat.

13
00:00:44.075 --> 00:00:47.246
It catches any exception
and turns it into Error,

14
00:00:47.246 --> 00:00:50.338
so a read that throws can
never come back as Pass.

15
00:00:50.338 --> 00:00:54.298
Don't catch exceptions inside the
body to make a check more robust;

16
00:00:54.298 --> 00:00:56.570
that's how a check passes while blind.
